    <item>
      <title>Ultrafast cellulose nanocrystal production from diverse lignocellulosic biomass</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01989-3</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Sustainability, Published online: 25 November 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01989-3"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01989-3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Producing cellulose nanocrystals conventionally involves hazardous chemicals, complex purification and high energy consumption. A recyclable hydrolytic quasi-solvent strategy now enables rapid production of cellulose nanocrystals from cellulose and untreated biomass with lower environmental impacts and costs.</content:encoded>
